.worktrees/

# Tool caches that collect at the repo root. There is no package.json here --
# the application lives in ctyhp-accounting/, which ignores its own -- so
# anything appearing here is a stray from a tool run, not a dependency.
node_modules/

# Shared Claude Code configuration is committed; the .local override is
# per-machine by convention and conflicts the moment two people share it.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Customer data used to exercise the importer. These exports carry real names,
# real bank descriptions, Zelle confirmation numbers and account balances, so
# they stay on the machine that needs them. Committing one is not a mistake you
# can take back: the file leaves the working tree easily and the history never.
data/

# The same data, arriving loose at the repo root rather than in data/. It does,
# repeatedly: a client's prototype lands here carrying two whole general ledgers
# inside it, an invoice export lands here carrying customer names and amounts.
# The rule above only helped the files that happened to be filed tidily, so these
# patterns cover the untidy ones. Nothing matching them is tracked today.
#
# The prototype has already been renamed once while sitting here, so match the
# stem rather than one filename.
/Accounting-System*.html
/*.beancount
/*.bean

# No CSV belongs at the repo root: the application, and every fixture it is
# allowed to commit, lives under ctyhp-accounting/. One that appears here came
# out of an accounting system and is somebody's real ledger.
/*.csv

# Output from test and gate runs. No log file is tracked anywhere in this repo,
# and a server log quotes the rows it served.
*.log

# Windows shell leftovers.
desktop.ini

# Loose HTML and Markdown at the repo root: the client's prototypes, review
# notes and side-by-side comparisons land here and carry real ledgers, customer
# names and sign-in addresses. They belong in data/, which is ignored above.
# One slipped past the /Accounting-System*.html rule by being saved with a
# space in its name, so match by extension. The coding guidebook is tracked and
# stays; tracked files are not affected by ignore rules.
/*.html
/*.md

# Transcripts of calls and screen recordings. One sat in docs/research/ for
# months: a colleague walking through the importer, by name. Research notes
# written from a call stay in docs/; the transcript itself goes in data/.
*transcript*.txt
*transcript*.vtt
*transcript*.srt

# An environment file at the repo root would hold the same keys as the app's,
# which ctyhp-accounting/ already ignores for itself.
/.env*
